# A subject of one letter and 997 blanks, 998 bytes, the most allowed.
# Blanks that end a value cannot be folded (a line break among them is the
# obsolete syntax), so the ones that do not fit on the line go out as
# encoded words of '_', after one blank that stands between the letter
# and the words: a reader turns the words back into the blanks and keeps
# that one, which gives the 997.  (subject-leading-blanks has them at the
# start, where a fold does.)
mode=accept
tls=none
form=(From=alice@example.com To=bob@example.net Body=$'Hi\n' User=alice Password=secret
      Subject="a$(printf ' %.0s' $(seq 997))")
